option.END_PLANETS.comment=One ringed giant, a faceted rift core with shard belts and a fixed starfield. End only.
option.END_ORBIT_SPEED.comment=0 freezes the planets; 0.5 / 1 / 2 changes orbital and axial speed.
option.PBR_MODE.comment=Auto reads packs declaring LabPBR. Use Force only with an undeclared LabPBR pack.
option.DOF_QUALITY.comment=For screenshots. Off by default.
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment=Camera motion only. Excludes hand pixels. Off by default.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Uses the temporally smoothed eye lightmap, with a bounded exposure gain.
option.SSR_QUALITY.comment=Off-screen rays fall back to sky or dim indoor environment.
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Sky reflection keeps water cheap; screen space adds traced hits on top for Ultra and Cinematic.
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=8192 consumes substantially more GPU memory.
option.TAA_QUALITY.comment=Reprojects HDR history with depth rejection and neighborhood clamping; FXAA remains optional.
option.SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=Medium and above use contact-hardening PCSS; Low uses a four-tap PCF fallback.
option.AO_QUALITY.comment=Directional horizon AO uses a world-space radius and edge-aware samples.
option.TONEMAP_MODE.comment=Natural Filmic preserves black levels, hue and soft highlights; ACES-like and the legacy curve remain available.
option.WEATHER_QUALITY.comment=Controls procedural rain layers, surface splashes and water ripples. Off restores the lightweight fallback.
option.TERRAIN_FOG_QUALITY.comment=Adds height, valley and distance fog with terrain depth occlusion.
option.RAIN_INTENSITY.comment=Scales procedural rain visibility without changing Minecraft weather state.
option.RIPPLE_STRENGTH.comment=Scales expanding rain rings on water and small impacts on exposed surfaces.
option.GODRAY_STRENGTH.comment=Scales shadow-mapped dawn and dusk shafts; midday is reduced automatically.
option.COLORED_LIGHT_QUALITY.comment=Screen-space colored light from emissive blocks. Voxel flood-fill is reserved for a later Iris compute pass.
option.COSMIC_SKY_QUALITY.comment=Galaxy band, nebulas, aurora and shooting stars in the Overworld night sky.
option.SEASON_MODE.comment=Auto follows the calendar year; manual modes force a season for screenshots or themed worlds.
option.SEASON_STRENGTH.comment=Blends seasonal sky, light, fog, cloud and foliage changes toward the vanilla look at zero.
option.CELESTIAL_EVENTS.comment=Calendar-driven meteor showers, comets, aurora storms, a solar eclipse and a rare supernova. Frequent compresses the schedule.
option.BIOME_BLEND.comment=Lets temperature and rainfall shift fog, haze and ambient colour: dry desert haze, humid jungle/swamp fog, cold blue tundra light.
option.PARTICLE_LAYER.comment=Procedural airborne particles: pollen and dust by day, fireflies at night, storm snow and hail, Nether embers and End motes.
option.CLOUD_TYPES.comment=Chooses cumulus, stratus, cirrus and storm anvil shapes from weather and season instead of one cloud field.
option.WEATHER_EFFECTS.comment=Adds desert sandstorms, cold-biome blizzards and low fog banks on top of the shared weather state.
option.SURFACE_SEASONS.comment=Winter frost/snow on top faces, patchier autumn leaves, rain puddles and summer heat shimmer.
